1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,952
I erase bad memories for a living, but today’s client broke my absolute rule.

2
00:00:06,252 --> 00:00:13,164
He slid a heavy gold coin across my desk and whispered, 'Take away the worst day of my life.'

3
00:00:13,464 --> 00:00:20,544
I plugged the silver extraction needle into his temple. The glowing blue memory thread flooded my screen.

4
00:00:20,844 --> 00:00:28,332
Bright sunlight, crashing ocean waves, and laughter. Wait, this isn't trauma. This is pure joy.

5
00:00:28,632 --> 00:00:34,680
Before I could pull the needle out, the memory surged forward and flooded my own neural implant.

6
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:42,636
I saw myself laughing on that beach, wearing a wedding ring, promising this exact stranger forever.

7
00:00:42,936 --> 00:00:49,968
The machine beeped. The extraction was complete. He opened his eyes and looked at me like a total stranger.

8
00:00:50,268 --> 00:00:56,052
'Who are you?' he asked politely, standing up and leaving the heavy gold coin on my desk.

9
00:00:56,352 --> 00:01:02,664
I reached for my own journal to figure out why I did this, but the pages were completely blank.

10
00:01:02,964 --> 00:01:11,820
I erased the pain of losing him, but in doing so, I lost him twice. If love leaves no scar, was it ever real?
